virglrenderer: a plain 2D view behind a 2D_ARRAY sampler

What: when a shader declares a sampler view 2D_ARRAY and the view bound there
is a plain 2D texture, that sampler is declared sampler2D in the GLSL and its
lookups take the 2D form (x and y; layer 0), as gallium reads such a view. A
key bit per view (sampler_views_2d_for_array_mask, the first 32 views) asks
for it, set only where the shader declares 2D_ARRAY (shader info
samplers_2d_array_mask), so other shaders' keys do not change; the view slot's
key bits (vrend_slot_key_bits) include it, so a 2D view coming or going there
selects the shaders again (virgl-legacy-vertex-cache.patch). A shader that
declares no sampler views at all (SAMP only) has the target only in its
lookups: there a 2D_ARRAY lookup counts as the 2D_ARRAY declaration of that
sampler. Not for samplers indexed indirectly.
Why: GL samples a 2D texture only through a sampler2D; a sampler2DArray on
that unit reads nothing (black). Mesa's VA-API video compositor declares its
plane samplers 2D_ARRAY while progressive video buffers are 2D textures, so
every frame VA-API converted to RGB was black (Google Chrome converts each
decoded frame so; FFmpeg's scale_vaapi gave Y=U=V=0 green with the colour
matrix fixed). Mesa's motion-adaptive deinterlacer (vl_deint_filter.c)
declares SAMP[0..3] without views and reads the decoded pictures, plain 2D
textures, with 2D_ARRAY lookups: every deinterlaced picture was Y=U=V=0,
green (mpv's vavpp default, FFmpeg's deinterlace_vaapi).
Upstreamable; not sent.
Tests: Tests/virgl/test-const-ubo.c case 23 (a 2D view through a 2D_ARRAY
sampler, alone and with constant buffer 0 as a guest buffer: black without
the patch), case 25 (the same lookup on a SAMP-only sampler, then a real 2D
array in that slot reading its layer 1: black without the SAMP-only part),
test-view-key.c (dirty tracking and the key bit with such a shader bound).
